"""Build a complete trial index from saved outcomes; never omit failed attempts."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];OUT=ROOT/'docs/brep/task-43'
def read(p,default):return json.loads(p.read_text()) if p.exists() else default
lines=['# Drawing checks and richer BRep generation','',
'Issues #24 and #43. Development target: `brep-integration`. `main` is unchanged.','',
'## Scope and interpretation of results','',
'The product now distinguishes build, geometry and drawing checks. It checks projections and openings in their required views. Exact radii, sections and preserved dimensions are measured independently in this benchmark. A passing build alone does not establish drawing fidelity. Product candidates remain unverified where view assignment or detailed features need review.','',
'The richer path saves a drawing-grounded construction plan before the recipe. It records planes, section shapes, dimensions, endpoint placement, connections, edit rules and unresolved assumptions. The plan is generated by the model; it is not a reference recipe or proof of correctness.','',
'Generation guidance distinguishes rounds from bevels, preserves sharp edge families and links useful parameters to dependent placements. Chamfer setback is converted to the kernel width across the bevel. Existing positive-overlap constraints cannot be weakened during correction.','',
'## Trial history','',
'All submitted BRep trials are listed below. Early failures, schema failures and kernel failures are retained. Changes between trials are development work, not independent statistical samples. No success rate or general superiority claim follows from this small development set.','',
'| Trial | Case | Run | Build | Independent original checks | Edit checks | Protected dimensions |',
'|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
for trial in sorted(OUT.glob('trial-*')):
 summary=read(trial/'summary.json',{});measurements=read(trial/'measurements.json',{})
 for name,case in summary.items():
  m=measurements.get(name,{})
  before=m.get('original',{}).get('status',m.get('status','not measured'))
  after=m.get('edited',{}).get('status','not measured')
  protected=m.get('protected_dimensions_passed','not measured')
  lines.append(f"| [{trial.name}]({trial.name}/summary.json) | {name} | `{case['id']}` | {case['status']} | {before} | {after} | {protected} |")
lines+=['','## Detailed evidence','',
'Each trial stores the submitted drawing and controls, input hash, job result, model responses, prompts, generated recipe, native 3D files and diagnostics. Successful product tests also store screenshots, edited recipe/STL/USDA, invalid-edit rejection and reload checks. Exact model settings are in [run-settings.json](run-settings.json); actual model identity and prompt versions are also in each generation record.','',
'Normal form controls and the drawing are generation inputs. The expected-feature contract, reference geometry and section measurements are not supplied to the model. The production checker contains no benchmark lookup.','']
for trial in sorted(OUT.glob('trial-*')):
 for name in ['handle','rounded','bevel']:
  target=trial/name
  if (target/'comparison.png').exists():
   lines += [f'### {name.title()} — {trial.name}','',f'![Actual input, generated part and edit]({trial.name}/{name}/comparison.png)','',f'[Measurements]({trial.name}/measurements.json) · [Product checks]({trial.name}/product-report.json) · [Saved artifacts]({trial.name}/{name}/artifacts)','']
lines+=['## Same-input OpenSCAD comparison','','These runs use the same drawings, empty notes and normal controls. They are a diagnostic comparison, not a benchmark of backend capability. A geometry that failed generation may still be constructible in OpenSCAD. No fallback result replaces a failed BRep candidate.','','| Case | Run | Existing evaluator accepted | Independent feature checks |','|---|---|---|---|']
for name,c in read(OUT/'openscad-comparison/comparison-report.json',{}).items():
 lines.append(f"| {name} | `{c.get('id')}` | {c.get('pipeline_accepted')} | {c.get('measurements',{}).get('status','not measured')} |")
lines+=['','[OpenSCAD raw trials and native SCAD/STL](openscad-comparison/summary.json) · [Comparison measurements](openscad-comparison/comparison-report.json)','',
'## Limits','','- General sweeps, lofts, hollow-body tools and face-selection editing are not added here.','- A construction plan can contain contradictions. It must be checked against the drawing and the resulting geometry.','- Native pipe unions can fail for near-coincident overlaps. Failed jobs publish no completed result.','- Projection checks are coarse and view assignment can be wrong. The app does not claim detailed drawing acceptance from those scores.','- Reload restores the original generation. Edited native files are saved, but the later revision-history task defines persistent selection of an edited revision.','- Synthetic engineering diagrams do not establish handwriting robustness. The bookend and other agreed regressions remain in the trial set.','',
'## Validation and reproduction','','See [tests.txt](tests.txt) for the final test run. Deterministic positive/negative geometry checks and their native files are in [task 07](../task-07/README.md). The browser tests verify geometry-changing parameters, matching downloads, invalid-edit rejection and original-result reload.','',
'```sh','python -m scripts.check_brep_drawing_features','python scripts/run_richer_brep_trials.py','python scripts/check_richer_brep_product.py','python -m scripts.measure_richer_brep','python scripts/render_richer_evidence.py','python -m scripts.check_openscad_rich_comparison','python scripts/report_richer_brep.py','```','',
'Use a separate BRep server and result directory. Set `DOODLE_TEST_URL`, `BREP_TRIAL` and optional `BREP_CASES` before a live run. Use a new trial directory for each rerun. Pin the isolated worker through `DOODLE_BREP_PYTHON`. Never change the saved thresholds to make a candidate pass.','']
(OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
print('Wrote',OUT/'REPORT.md')
